Based on my analysis of the panoramic radiograph — examining each apical region at high magnification with contrast enhancement — I identified three areas of periapical bone change (diffuse/mottled reduced bone density around root apices, without sharply corticated margins, consistent with PAI 3). The posterior mandibular regions bilaterally and the lower anterior periapical zone all show these changes; the well-defined appearance of the submandibular fossa and other normal radiolucencies was excluded.

